# Table grid commands

Handle `$ARGUMENTS`. Active Local CI gate running the real `BaseTablePlugin` (`allowCellSpanEditing: true`) across every span layout up to 3x3 against an independent layout oracle.

**The property.** After any table insert, remove, merge, split, cell edit, paste, or picked-cell command on any span layout up to 3x3, every slot belongs to exactly one cell and cell content matches the Table section of `docs/editor-behavior/markdown-editing-spec.md`.

**The harm.** A broken span grid draws cells in wrong columns, drops cells, or moves user content into the wrong cell.

## Run it

- `pnpm check table-grid` (active Local CI gate; `--light` runs the same gate, ~65 s p90): 14,471 cases across 411 layouts (`GATE_CASES`).
- `pnpm check:table-grid --all`: all commands at all cells/pairs (56,840 cases, skips baseline).
- `pnpm check:table-grid --rows=<r> --cols=<c>` or `--case='<id>'`: raise bounds or print stack for matching cases.
- `pnpm check:table-grid --lower`: shrink `packages/platejs/scripts/table-grid-commands-baseline.json` (currently 0 findings).

Exit 0 passes, 1 reports findings (`table-grid`, `table-content`, `table-throws`), 2 reports bad flag or crashed worker.

## Bounds and assumptions

- Tests `insertRow`, `insertColumn`, `removeRow`, `removeColumn`, `split`, `merge` (+ type after merge), Enter, Backspace, Delete, 2-paragraph paste, cross-cell delete, and picked-cell delete/type/paste without calling `compileTableGrid`.
- Excludes tables >3x3, nested tables, direct-text Plite cells, headers/styling/resizing, `allowCellSpanEditing: false`, pasted tables, cross-table ranges, caret placement, undo/redo, direct `editorCommands.delete` on picked cells, and browser events.

## Bug vs drift

- **Real bug:** command breaks slot coverage or moves content against the spec's Table section. Fix plugin/Plite owner and run `--lower`.
- **Modeling error / intended change:** update `packages/platejs/scripts/table-grid-commands.ts` and the spec's Table section together; never weaken a law or grow baseline.

## Coverage record

Synced at `test(platejs): check that every table command keeps a valid grid on every small span layout`. Check drift with `git log --oneline <commit>..HEAD -- packages/platejs/src/features/table packages/platejs/scripts/table-grid-commands.ts`; move sync commit only after confirming script and passing `pnpm check:table-grid`.

Covered paths: `packages/platejs/src/features/table/lib/BaseTablePlugin.ts`, `packages/platejs/src/features/table/lib/internal/{mutation,grid,selection}.ts`, `packages/plitejs/src/core/{editor-commands,node-selection}.ts`, `packages/plitejs/src/transforms-text/delete-text-grid.ts`.

Use `/pstack:maintain-formal-verification-skill` after changes that skipped this check.
